      "lyrics": "Verse 1\nMorning broke in a flicker on the TV wall\nAnother city whispering through the static call\nCoffee getting colder on the windowsill\nEverybody talking but the room stood still\n\nSirens in the distance, headlines in a chain\nNumbers like a shadow running through the rain\nWe laughed it off at first like weather passing through\nBut the sky turned gray in a different shade of blue\n\nPre-Chorus\nSomething in the air tonight\nSomething in the way we lock the door\nHolding on to normal life\nLike we\u2019ve ever held it before\n\nChorus\nWarning lights, flashing over every street\nRed signs, pulsing with a broken beat\nWe don\u2019t know where we\u2019re going\nBut we feel the ground start rolling\nWarning lights, burning through the darkened glass\nClosed eyes, praying that it doesn\u2019t last\nWe keep watching the horizon\nWhile the whole world\u2019s siren cries in\nWarning lights\n\nVerse 2\nEmpty trains were moving like a ghost parade\nNeon in the windows where the people stayed\nPhones lit up like candles in our shaking hands\nTrying to understand what no one understands\n\nShelves went bare by midnight, doors began to close\nNeighbors kept their distance in their winter coats\nEvery little cough became a loaded gun\nAnd the streets forgot the sound of everyone\n\nPre-Chorus\nSomething in the air tonight\nSomething in the quiet after noise\nWe were standing at the borderline\nBetween the life we knew and the void\n\nChorus\nWarning lights, flashing over every street\nRed signs, pulsing with a broken beat\nWe don\u2019t know where we\u2019re going\nBut we feel the ground start rolling\nWarning lights, burning through the darkened glass\nClosed eyes, praying that it doesn\u2019t last\nWe keep watching the horizon\nWhile the whole world\u2019s siren cries in\nWarning lights\n\nBridge\nHold your breath, don\u2019t look away\nThe future\u2019s changing shape\nAll the plans we made\nAre paper in the rain\nHold the line, stay awake\nFeel the old world shake\nIf tomorrow calls our names\nWill we answer the same?\n\nFinal Chorus\nWarning lights, flashing over every street\nRed signs, pulsing with a broken beat\nWe don\u2019t know where we\u2019re going\nBut we feel the ground start rolling\nWarning lights, burning through the darkened glass\nClosed eyes, praying that it doesn\u2019t last\nWe keep watching the horizon\nWhile the whole world\u2019s siren cries in\nWarning lights\n\nOutro\nMorning broke in a flicker on the TV wall\nWe didn\u2019t know it then\nWe were losing it all\nWarning lights in the window\nWarning lights in the sky\nSomething was ending\nAnd we didn\u2019t know why",
