      "lyrics": "Verse 1\n\nForks hit plates like warning shots\nSunday dinner getting loud\nUncle's got a headline loaded\nMama's staring at the ground\nCousin says, \u201cYou\u2019re blind to reason\u201d\nDaddy says, \u201cYou\u2019ve lost your mind\u201d\nEverybody came for comfort\nEverybody picked a side\n\nPre-Chorus\n\nAnd the TV in the corner keeps preaching to the flame\nAll the voices in our pockets keep calling us by name\nI don\u2019t know what\u2019s real, I don\u2019t know who to trust\nWhen every little truth gets torn in two by us\n\nChorus\n\nWho came here to divide the room?\nTurn our blood into red and blue\nMake a stranger out of me and you\nWho came here to divide the room?\nWe\u2019re shouting over silver spoons\nDancing with a lit fuse\nI still love you, but I hate what we\u2019ve become\nWho came here to divide the room?\n\nVerse 2\n\nScreens glow like a midnight trial\nEverybody\u2019s got a case\nAlgorithms sell us anger\nWith a pretty filter face\nOne link leads into a landslide\nOne lie learns to sound like fact\nWe were kids in the same backyard\nNow we don\u2019t know how to get back\n\nPre-Chorus\n\nAnd the silence after midnight feels heavier than war\nWe keep typing out our damage, then we beg for something more\nI don\u2019t know what\u2019s real, I don\u2019t know where it starts\nWhen every breaking story breaks another heart\n\nChorus\n\nWho came here to divide the room?\nTurn our blood into red and blue\nMake a stranger out of me and you\nWho came here to divide the room?\nWe\u2019re shouting over silver spoons\nDancing with a lit fuse\nI still love you, but I hate what we\u2019ve become\nWho came here to divide the room?\n\nBridge\n\nCan we turn it off for a minute?\nCan we breathe before we burn?\nCan we ask a better question\nThan who wins and whose turn?\nIf the truth is buried somewhere\nUnder panic, pride, and pain\nWill we dig with open hands\nOr throw the dirt and call it blame?\n\nFinal Chorus\n\nWho came here to divid